# Cloudflare cache rules.
#
# Lesson learned: NEVER put `immutable` on a file whose name doesn't change
# when its contents change. `immutable` tells the browser to never revalidate
# — so an edited home.css / hero3d.js keeps serving the stale cached copy
# (you can't even hard-refresh it away on iOS Safari). Instead we revalidate:
# the browser sends a conditional request, Cloudflare returns a tiny 304 when
# nothing changed, and the moment a file changes the browser picks it up.
# Bandwidth is unmetered on Cloudflare, so the revalidation round-trips are free.

# Everything: revalidate every load (ETag → 304 when unchanged) + security headers.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Content-Security-Policy notes — every host above is one the site genuinely
# loads: googletagmanager (GA4), jsdelivr (supabase-js), unpkg (three.js +
# the meshopt decoder, which is WASM, hence wasm-unsafe-eval), Google Fonts,
# and the Supabase project for data. 'unsafe-inline' is required because the
# GA snippet and several page scripts are inline. If anything on the site
# stops working after deploy, delete the Content-Security-Policy line and
# redeploy — nothing else depends on it.

# Images and the 3D model rarely change — let them sit briefly to cut
# round-trips, but NO `immutable`, so they still self-heal within the hour.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
